WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.501
-It is so awesome to have you
on the show

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.734
just because, you know,
we're big fans.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.601
You've been on the show
a bunch of times,

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:08.601
but today is actually
your record is out!

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.100
-It's out.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.400
[ Cheering and applause ]
Thank you.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:14.434
The odds of us seeing --
I'm so happy to witness this.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:16.300
-I'm honored to see you
the day of.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.367
-Yeah!
-It's a good luck charm, maybe.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:19.234
-Yes, it is!
-Yeah.

00:00:19.234 --> 00:00:20.434
-It's finally out.

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.067
Let's look at it right here.
"Humble Quest."

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.968
-That's her.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.601
-Alright.
I want to talk about the title.

00:00:26.601 --> 00:00:28.100
I want to talk about the photo.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.501
What's the photo?
How'd you decide on this cover?

00:00:31.501 --> 00:00:33.267
-Well, it was the last setup
of the day

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:36.400
and it was in this
like high school basement gym.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.267
And so I was like, "Yeah,
I guess we'll do it,

00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:41.601
if it's here."
But it was heated.

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.067
-So this is just a pool
in a high school

00:00:43.067 --> 00:00:45.467
and you jumped in?
-Yeah. I mean, they let me in.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:46.801
[ Laughter ]
-No, yeah. You didn't break in.

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.267
Yeah, you didn't break, yeah.
-No.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:50.901
But it actually, it just ended
up being one of my favorites

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.868
because it wasn't like overdone
and my hair's wet

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:57.734
and it felt kind of like
baptismal, in a way.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:00.067
So it fit the vibe
of the music, So.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:04.367
-And "Humble Quest,"
which is the name of the album.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.901
What does that mean,
humble quest?

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.334
-Well, I feel like
the last two years

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:11.334
were probably humbling
for all humans,

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:15.200
just not having jobs
or just not having a purpose.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.567
And I had my son at the very
beginning of the pandemic,

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:23.067
so that cut me down
a little bit, too.

00:01:23.067 --> 00:01:26.601
I had kind of a rough
like delivery and so,

00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:29.968
yeah, having my son
and then having touring canceled

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:33.367
for two years was just like
I'm celebrating my baby,

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:35.634
but I can't like share him
with anybody

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:38.834
because we're quarantining
and then I couldn't tour.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.834
So it was just like
a really grounding experience,

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.133
learning that like --
Like I love what I do.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.834
I've been doing music
since I was ten,

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.534
but I put so much
of my worth in it

00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:51.801
and I think the last two years
taught me that

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.834
like I can love what I do,

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.968
but I don't have to do it
to feel loved,

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:57.534
if that makes sense.
-Yeah.

00:01:57.534 --> 00:01:59.067
[ Cheering and applause ]
Good for you.

00:01:59.067 --> 00:02:00.601
You got through it.
You got through it

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.901
and you have a beautiful baby.
-Yes.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.067
-Beautiful baby boy.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:06.334
And I actually love,
on one of the tracks,

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.567
I think it's "Hummingbird,"
maybe...
-Yeah.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.334
-...he's on.
He says, "Mama."

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:12.434
-Yeah.

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.200
-It's very cute.
It's awesome.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.033
-I actually wrote "Hummingbird"
the day I found out

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:20.400
I was having my son back in 2019
and then the pandemic hit,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.434
I had him, and then, by the time
I was recording this record,

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:25.767
my son was starting to talk.

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:28.934
And so I got a little iPhone
voice recording

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:32.133
of him saying "Mama," and so
Greg Kurstin, my producer,

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.234
put it at the top of that song.

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:37.067
It's actually the only feature
on the record, is my son.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.133
[ Laughter ]
-Featuring, yeah.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:39.834
He got a feature credit, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.067
-The Grammys are next weekend.
You're nominated for two awards.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.934
Congratulations on that.
-Thanks.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:48.100
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.334
-You meet a lot of people.

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.467
You've done collaborations
with everyone cool.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.901
I mean, gosh,
you're just amazing already,

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.901
your career,
and you're still so young.

00:02:55.901 --> 00:02:58.934
But Dolly, just to say,
just to start there.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:00.801
Taylor.
But I was like,

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:03.167
is there anyone that really like
blows your mind

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:07.100
and you freak out
and you fangirl out?

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:08.634
-I feel like twice in my life

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:12.434
I've been starstruck
by somebody and like one --

00:03:12.434 --> 00:03:14.334
Well, actually three.
One was Dolly,

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:17.634
the other was Elton John,
like meeting him, and then --

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:18.501
-[ Clears throat ]

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:21.334
[ Laughter ]
-I was --

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.501
And Jimothy Fallon.
-Thank you.

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:24.934
-Yeah, sorry.
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.367
Sorry.
-Starstruck, yes.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:27.901
-My God! Okay.
-The four people.

00:03:27.901 --> 00:03:28.567
-[Both] Yeah.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.367
-But no. Okay.

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.834
The fourth would be

00:03:32.834 --> 00:03:35.300
I was at this Beatles
documentary party

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.801
at Henson Studios in L.A.
a couple of months ago

00:03:37.801 --> 00:03:40.567
and I was leaving early
because that's like my move

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:43.334
-[ Laughs ]
-and I saw Amy Poehler doing

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:44.868
the exact same thing.
[ Awws and laughter ]

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:48.467
And I had a couple
margaritas in me,

00:03:48.467 --> 00:03:51.033
but I never do this,
but I was like,

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:53.434
"I will regret if I don't go
up to her and just say like

00:03:53.434 --> 00:03:54.834
how much she means to me."

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.534
And especially like just
growing up watching "SNL"

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.033
with you guys on it

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:02.367
and just how much she means
to me as a woman who is funny.

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:04.868
And I go over to her
and she's so sweet

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.601
like I'm sure you know

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:07.901
because you know her.
-She's the greatest.

00:04:07.901 --> 00:04:10.567
-But I was just like bawling,
and I was like,

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:12.267
"I know you don't know who I am,

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:13.767
but I'm such a huge fan of yours

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:15.234
and thank you,
blah, blah, blah."

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:17.567
And she was like,
"I know who you are."

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:19.000
[ Laughter ]
It's like, "Yeah,
you're Maren Morris.

00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:20.367
I mean, you're pretty famous."

00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:22.367
Here's a picture
of you guys together.
-Yeah.

00:04:22.367 --> 00:04:24.534
[ Awws and applause ]
-I look like I need
to be sedated.

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:25.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:28.033
-Amy is the best.
-Yeah, she is.

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:28.934
-She's a good one.

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.167
-Someone sedate this girl

00:04:31.167 --> 00:04:33.067
that is bothering Amy Poehler.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:36.000
Yeah. I have tears in my eyes
in the photo.
-Yeah, good.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.000
"Humble Quest" -- Congrats.
It's record day.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.234
I'm so happy it's out.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.067
Everyone download it,
whatever you got to do.

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.734
Buy this album.

00:04:42.734 --> 00:04:45.467
And you're actually going
on tour this summer.

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.000
-Yeah. Yeah.
-It's all happening, bud.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.467
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.234
-Thank you.
Thanks.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.667
I'm playing Radio City, so.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:55.868
-You are coming.
-I'll be across the way.

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.667
-I'm there! I'm so there.
-Alright.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.467
-I will be onstage if you want.
I love you.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:02.267
[ Laughter ]
What song are you doing
for us tonight?

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:04.767
I'm going to do my song
"Circles Around This Town," so.

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.067
-There you go.
I'm so happy you're here.

00:05:07.067 --> 00:05:09.400
We love you.
Maren Morris, everybody!

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:12.968
[ Cheering and applause ]
Congrats. "Humble Quest"
is out right now!

